    },
    {
      "source_page_url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Touch_Change%21_%28Garura_Parent/Child_promo%29",
      "line": 146,
      "text": "タッチ交代！ Touch Change!"
    },
    {
      "source_page_url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Touch_Change%21_%28Garura_Parent/Child_promo%29",
      "line": 147,
      "text": "Illus. Nobuyuki Habu"
    },
    {
      "source_page_url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Touch_Change%21_%28Garura_Parent/Child_promo%29",
      "line": 151,
      "text": "Touch Change! (Japanese: タッチ交代！ Touch Change!) is a Trainer card. It is one of the Unnumbered Promotional cards."
    },
    {
      "source_page_url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Touch_Change%21_%28Garura_Parent/Child_promo%29",
      "line": 188,
      "text": "This card was given to participants of the Garura Parent/Child Tournament in May 1998, as it was necessary for the Garura Rules version of the TCG utilized in the tournament. While not included as part of a 60-card deck, the card was still part of it, and had no effect when not playing by Garura Rules."
    },
    {
      "source_page_url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Touch_Change%21_%28Garura_Parent/Child_promo%29",
      "line": 190,
      "text": "The Garura Parent/Child Tournament involved teams of parents and their children battling similar teams. Teams that won a certain number of battles over the course of the event were awarded with the now sought after Kangaskhan promotional card."
    },
    {
      "source_page_url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Kangaskhan_%28Garura_Parent/Child_promo%29",
      "line": 144,
      "text": "Kangaskhan LV.38"
    },
    {
      "source_page_url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Kangaskhan_%28Garura_Parent/Child_promo%29",
      "line": 145,
      "text": "ガルーラ Garura"
    },
    {
      "source_page_url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Kangaskhan_%28Garura_Parent/Child_promo%29",
      "line": 167,
      "text": "Kangaskhan (Japanese: ガルーラ Garura) is a Colorless-type Basic Pokémon card. It is one of the Unnumbered Promotional cards."
    },
    {
      "source_page_url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Kangaskhan_%28Garura_Parent/Child_promo%29",
      "line": 199,
      "text": "In Japan, this card was released through the Parent/Child Mega Battle tournament held in May 1998. The prize was awarded to those parent and children teams who had reached a certain number of wins. This card is one of few promotional cards to feature the original Pocket Monsters Card Game logo."
    },
    {
